WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
Leave a metal block and a wooden
block in a cold room overnight.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.900
In the morning, touch them both.

3
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.920
The metal feels icy.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.620
The wood hardly feels cold at all.

5
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.350
Your fingers seem to give a clear answer.

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.130
But is the metal really at a
lower temperature than the wood?

7
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.610
In this mission, you'll see which way
energy flows when a hot object touches a

8
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.780
cold one.

9
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.580
Then you'll look inside a material,
at the random motion of its particles,

10
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.790
and find out what
temperature really measures.

11
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.170
Your mission: find out whether the metal
is really at a lower temperature than

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:36.830
the wood.
